1|0@baseball^1440092714#cu9pg3b:ObligatoryHandle$:I'll make no argument that Ryno does not have he edge on defense. But I will say that there was a sense that fielding stats and Gold Glove voters didn't properly appreciate Utley during his peak. The Fielding Bible was thought to see it better, with Utley finishing Top 5 every year from 2006-10 and winning once. [Here](http://www.fieldingbible.com/the-2010-winners.asp) is the write-up for his 2010 win. It speaks to that sense: &gt; Finally! After being atop the three-year Runs Saved leader board in each of the last four years, Chase Utley wins his first Fielding Bible Award in 2010. Utley has saved 60 runs with his defense for the Phillies in the last three years. Far behind him are Mark Ellis (33), Dustin Pedroia (30) and Aaron Hill (26). In the voting, Orlando Hudson gave Chase a run for his money, falling just six points short (80 points compared to 86 for Utley). Hudson did have three more runs saved than Utley in 2010 (17 to 14), but Chase’s consistency over many years was rewarded by the voters. Now the question is, can Utley win his first Gold Glove award?
