1|0@baseball^1440076190#cu9f5j4:raszama$:I think Utley is going to go down in history much the same way that Don Mattingly did. Arguably the best player at their position for 3-5 years, All-Star, potential MVP candidate. Both suffered injuries that really derailed their careers fairly young (early 30's). Looking at their stats, pretty much the only difference is that systems love Utley's defense and hate Mattingly's, and obviously Utley played the much more valuable position on the diamond. I don't think Utley's career is over. This is basically the first year he's been below replacement, and most of that is due to injuries. I would not be surprised if he bounced back next year (or even at the end of this one) and put up a few more 2-3 WAR seasons. If he does that, I think he's in. If his career ended this year, I'd say he's borderline, but I think I would vote for him. Sustained high peak &gt; tack on years.
